ease that was healthy in production. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reports VERIFIED, with all three regions on v2.3.0. Next steps: confirm error rate and health checks recover, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.", "confidence": 0.9, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** The most recent production release that was healthy was v2.3.0. v2.3.1 was unhealthy and running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 0.18. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, and the rollback reports as verified.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open at SEV2. Its summary records the failure, the rollback target, and the regions affected.\n\nI haven't re-checked the service status since the rollback, so recovery of health checks and error rate is still unconfirmed. The incident also lists investigating v2.3.1 before it is released again as a next step.", "type": "text"}]}]}